A:
To check if a string is a palindrome (reads the same forwards and backwards), you can simply loop through half of the string and compare each character with its counterpart from the end of the string. Here's a Python function to do this:

```python
def is_palindrome(s):
    for i in range(len(s)):
        if s[i] != s[len(s) - 1 - i]:  
            return False
    return True
```

This function will return `True` if all characters up to the middle match their mirrored counterparts and `False` otherwise. Note that it considers case sensitivity but can be adjusted accordingly.

